==Trivia==
*The name Sathankhamun is a combination of ''Satan'' (the inspiration for [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] and his variants, whom Sathankhamun's mask also resembles), 仮面 ''kamen'' (mask) and ''[[wikipedia:Tutankhamun|Tutankhamun]]'' (an Egyptian pharaoh whose mask is very well known).
*Like [[Wicked Face]], Sathankhamun VIII's design is most likely a reference to Big Ben and Little Ben, the demon-costumed bacteria seen in some of TOTO's [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wag1pjUya94 toilet commercials].
*Its Japanese description contains the fourth reference to a "demon king" in [[The Battle Cats]], the first being [[Cat Clan Heroes (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Clan Heroes]]' Japanese description, the second being [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]]'s description and the third being [[Possessed by Evil (Merciless)|Possessed by Evil]]'s Japanese name (Possessed by the Demon King). These likely refer to [[Infernal Tyrant Nyandam]], who indeed returned in the form he took when he ruled the world 560,000 years ago, and whose Japanese name is Great Demon King Nyandam.
*Based on its role in the Great Aku's return, Sathankhamun VIII may represent the Antichrist, who is sometimes interpreted as a human vessel in which Satan will [[Aku Reincarnation (Merciless)|incarnate]]. In fact, the [[Media:Aku Reincarnation Event Poster JP.png|Japanese event poster]] for Rashomon uses the phrase ''Maō no Keshin'' (魔王の化身), which literally translates to "Incarnation of the Demon King" or "Incarnation of Satan". Moreover, one of the figures identified with the Antichrist is the eighth king in the Book of Revelation, explaining Sathankhamun VIII's name - it sounds similar to Tutankhamun, a king, and contains the Roman numeral VIII (eight).
**In the Bible, the number eight is also associated with new beginnings, regeneration and resurrection, which correlates with Sathankhamun VIII's involvement in the second coming of the Great Aku.
*Within the context of Rashomon, Sathankhamun VIII may represent [[wikipedia:Rashōmon no oni|Rashōmon no oni]], an ''[[wikipedia:Oni|oni]]'' (a type of demon-like ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'') said to have lived at the gate [[wikipedia:Rajōmon|Rashōmon]]. Sathankhamun VIII is a variant of [[Hannya]], whose Japanese description refers to her as an ''oni''.

